SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Artillery ***\nSoldi
 ers: Artillery\, Brigade\, Infantry — Costume (you provide): Black Sea
 mless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard Male Soldiers: Black T-shirt\, Bla
 ck tights\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hai
 r: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): White Gloves\; Prop (
 BA provides): Brown gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powd
 er matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease w
 ith an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara
 . No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so d
 ancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Re
 d lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone b
 allet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with c
 are while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly n
 otify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of dis
 covery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessor
 ies on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain
  from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter
 \, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply s
 tage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from 
 smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use
  of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garmen
 t not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beve
 rage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove c
 ostumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remo
 ve all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their us
 e\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully wi
 th any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do n
 ot pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or
  stain costumes.
